entifying the Polynomial Given its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d53b85c7-a6cb-55cb-a0a6-c9a46039e689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{6}-3{x}^{2}-3x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242939} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa5fd26-b63a-50c7-846e-8d09bc942483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242940} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1fcce3-2aa1-5e9a-b214-af8b9c7bf171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{5}-6{x}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242941} {:answer/id #uuid "138bbae8-8c46-5734-ab43-c2177e9667ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7{x}^{9}+4{x}^{5}-8{x}^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242942} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1d0cc0-367b-54fe-b903-d094a58f7ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f1fcce3-2aa1-5e9a-b214-af8b9c7bf171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{5}-6{x}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242941} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f2c402-85bf-542d-af8c-78473922a23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "426e55d1-c90c-5ab3-939e-cd136ab31aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-112098" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13928579/assets/aad161b50958b85f30421bf7420faf87ff4dc291ca1bb6d233626d67a42885ba.png)\n\nWhich of the following polynomials could be the function shown in the diagram above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's call $P(x)$ the polynomial shown in the diagram.\n\nThe end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is positive.\n\n- the $y$-intercept is $3,$ which means that $P(0)=3.$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the only one that satisfies all three criteria is $y=2{x}^{5}-6{x}^{2}+3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d04e66-3d88-5940-b1c0-aa82db7b420a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242946} {:answer/id #uuid "c427ec8a-ee9b-5f20-9b09-1afc54326600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242947} {:answer/id #uuid "8a616b5f-36f4-5d3e-be91-7c303a8f3ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242948} {:answer/id #uuid "badc6577-e6ef-57a9-93d5-15cac5a51f1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242949} {:answer/id #uuid "b04527f2-31b9-5810-b52a-085e462f9102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c427ec8a-ee9b-5f20-9b09-1afc54326600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242947} :answer-field/id #uuid "68fd18e2-ea87-531c-97de-e722e54117cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8ee49b2-e7b5-5264-be76-f69838febcea" :question/math-academy-id "q-112114" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13928579/assets/b46093feaf5d7138e30c6d6fc673a2d915cac74a23ae76e0841e9bb5b135fa60.png)\n\nThe graph of the polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The degree of $P(x)$ is even.\n- The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n- The constant term is positive." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nSo, statement I is true, while statement II is false.\n\nLastly, note that the $y$-intercept is positive, and therefore the constant term must be positive. So, III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c28e34da-550d-562f-91ae-a158550abd2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242953} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cb2fe9-6261-5e9e-8f41-7f373ab48c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242954} {:answer/id #uuid "f673a7e6-c977-51aa-9108-9d5b03b0ee39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242955} {:answer/id #uuid "03591125-67e4-5e62-a87c-fae2fed7936c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242956} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f49a7d-110c-5ecd-b2a3-cb07f838a0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4cb2fe9-6261-5e9e-8f41-7f373ab48c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :ans